-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Derived data — CC BY-SA 4.0
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Applies to exactly these three files:

    game-words.js
    phonetics-data.js
    phonetics-kanji-index.js

Each carries kanji phonetic-component data derived from Kanjium, which is
licensed CC BY-SA 4.0. ShareAlike is inherited by adaptations, so these files
are offered under the same licence and not under the MIT terms above. Anyone
redistributing them, modified or not, must do so under CC BY-SA 4.0 and keep
the attribution below.

    Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

    Contains data from Kanjium by Uros Ozvald and contributors
    https://github.com/mifunetoshiro/kanjium — CC BY-SA 4.0

phonetics-data.js additionally carries usage-frequency ranking derived from
scriptin/kanji-frequency (CC BY 4.0), and phonetics-kanji-index.js is generated
from phonetics-data.js.

The remaining data files — mnjp-data.js, reading-texts.js and
dictionary-data.js — carry no Kanjium-derived material and are covered by
section 1, subject to the third-party notices in section 3.


